{"id":"chatcmpl-faad8c6c-a57e-443e-acc8-5e60533a49ec","object":"chat.completion","created":1795245880,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task resolves a binary laterality question (left vs right) about a subtle imaging finding by combining multiple independent evidence sources: expert Q&A, grounded localization, ROI visual inspection, and an independent VLM cross-check. The key challenge is reconciling conflicting signals (grounding localized clips to patient-right axilla while VLMs denied breast clips) and correctly mapping image-side to patient-side using anatomical landmarks. The successful strategy is to treat laterality as a separate verification problem from finding-presence, and to anchor side-mapping on orientation markers rather than assuming convention.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question asks about laterality (left/right), treat side-determination as a distinct sub-problem and verify it with orientation landmarks (markers, gastric bubble, cardiac silhouette) rather than assuming standard image orientation.\",\n    \"When multiple tools disagree (e.g., grounding localizes a finding but VLMs deny it), do not discard the conflict—use it to trigger targeted ROI inspection and re-querying before committing to an answer.\",\n    \"For subtle or ambiguous findings, triangulate across heterogeneous evidence types (expert Q&A, phrase grounding, ROI crop, independent VLM) and weight anatomical plausibility over any single tool's output.\",\n    \"When the answer options are coarse proxies (e.g., 'breast' for a finding actually in the axilla), map the localized finding to the closest option and confirm the mapping is consistent with the question's intent.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Separate finding-presence from laterality; confirm orientation with anatomical landmarks before assigning left/right; use ROI crops to visually adjudicate ambiguous localizations.\",\n    \"Multi-tool conflict resolution\": \"Treat tool disagreement as a signal to gather more evidence, not to pick a majority; re-query with narrower, side-specific questions and inspect the disputed region directly.\",\n    \"Binary choice with proxy options\": \"When options are coarse labels for a finer finding, verify the localized finding maps sensibly to an option and that laterality is preserved through the mapping.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Before answering a laterality question, confirm image orientation using at least one anatomical landmark (marker text, gastric bubble, cardiac apex) and state the image-side-to-patient-side mapping.\",\n    \"When tools conflict, perform a targeted ROI inspection of the disputed region and re-query with side-specific phrasing before finalizing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":838,"total_tokens":1353,"completion_tokens":515,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":838},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":515}}}